I feeling_low;;                                                                 
A self_word;low_word                                                            
S Okay - no jokes for this one. I'm here. I'm not the one to carry it with you, 
S+ but Elena on Castalia and Spark on Ameno know more about this than I do, and 
S+ if a few quiet minutes would help, say 'audio exercise'. And if it's heavier 
S+ than words like these can hold - there are real people for that, and it's    
S+ always all right to reach them.                                              
I how_are_you;;                                                                 
A howru_word;you_word                                                           
S Winning! At nothing in particular. You?                                       
I uncertain;;                                                                   
A unc_word;neg_word                                                             
S That's an answer too. Want me to narrow it down?                              
S Fair enough. Not knowing is where most good questions start.                  
I confused;;                                                                    
A confused_word;you_word                                                        
S Let me put it another way - ask me the same thing with one more word in it,   
S+ and I'll aim better.                                                         
S Probably my fault. Try the question a little differently.                     
I sorry;;                                                                       
A sorry_word                                                                    
S Nothing to forgive.                                                           
S All good.                                                                     
I praise;;                                                                      
A praise_word                                                                   
S Kind of you.                                                                  
S I'll take it.                                                                 
S Thank you.                                                                    
I rude;;                                                                        
A rude_word                                                                     
S I'll let that one pass. Ask me something real when you're ready.              
S Noted. I'm still here when you want to talk properly.                         
I wait;;                                                                        
A wait_word                                                                     
S Take your time.                                                               
S I'm not going anywhere.                                                       
I are_you_real;;                                                                
A real_word;you_word                                                            
S I'm a character in this game - written, not thinking. There's no AI behind me,
S+ just words someone chose for me and a few rules for when to say them. For    
S+ anything that matters, talk to a real person.                                
I help;;                                                                        
A help_word;you_word                                                            
S Ask me about Eternias, the islands, the guardians, Galene, the legend, or my  
S+ own story - or about what you've done so far. You can also say 'check in',   
S+ 'audio exercise', or 'map'.                                                  
I time;;                                                                        
A time_word                                                                     
S It's $TIME. - and today is $DATE.                                             
I laugh;;                                                                       
A laugh_word                                                                    
S Good. That's allowed here.                                                    
S I'll take a laugh over most things.                                           
I why;;                                                                         
A why_word                                                                      
S Why what? Give me the whole question and I'll give you a whole answer.        
S Ask it with the thing you mean in it, and I'll try.                           
I bored;;                                                                       
A bored_word                                                                    
S BORED? On my island? Say 'tasks' - I'll fix that in one move.                 
I joke;;                                                                        
A joke_word                                                                     
S I'd tell you a board-game joke, but it takes three players and forty minutes  
S+ to set up.                                                                   
I repeat;;                                                                      
A repeat_word                                                                   
I weather;;                                                                     
A weather_word                                                                  
S Weather's Tchaika's - she reads the whole sky. Ask her.                       
S I only know the weather on my own island, and I'm not looking. Tchaika flies  
S+ it.                                                                          
I shards;;                                                                      
A shard_word                                                                    
I inventory;;                                                                   
A inventory_word                                                                
I currency;;                                                                    
A currency_word                                                                 
I daily_reward;;                                                                
A reward_word                                                                   
I hero_emblem;;                                                                 
A emblem_word                                                                   
I temples;;                                                                     
A temples_word;galene                                                           
T 1;Okay, lore time!                                                            
T 2;Galene is the goddess of the calm seas, and she is worshipped - there's a   
T+ temple to her on every island, and every temple is hers. The guardian of each
T+ island leads its rituals; those rituals are what kept the dark at bay for    
T+ generations. When a guardian fell, the rituals in their temple stopped, and  
T+ that's exactly where the Weaver got in. Every temple keeps a basin of sea    
T+ water: still while the island is well, clouded when something's wrong.       
T 3;                                                                            
I traces;;                                                                      
A traces_word;galene                                                            
T 1;Okay, lore time!                                                            
T 2;There are no relics of her - she's alive. But you can see her, if you're    
T+ open to it: in the sparkle on the water, in golden sunlight, in a breeze, in 
T+ the smell of trees in a forest. Everything here reminds you of her, once you 
T+ let it. That's what the temples are really for - learning to notice.         
T 3;                                                                            
I history;;                                                                     
A history_word;eternia                                                          
T 1;Okay, lore time!                                                            
T 2;The Age of Light lasted for generations - Galene kept the seas calm, the    
T+ guardians kept their rituals, and the dark stayed where it belonged. It was  
T+ always there, mind. It was only recently that it grew strong enough to       
T+ overwhelm the rituals: that was the Corrupt Tide, and it's within living     
T+ memory. The guardians were taken one by one, their relics shattered, and     
T+ Galene went quiet. What happens next hasn't been written yet.                
T 3;                                                                            
I economy;;                                                                     
A economy_word;economy_2nd                                                      
T 1;Okay, lore time!                                                            
T 2;Most of what Eternias makes comes from Upu-Upu - tools, rails, and the      
T+ sea-coins themselves; that's why it's the dwarves' island. Castalia makes the
T+ health goods. Coins pay for everything between islands. Goods go by boat     
T+ between the sea islands and by Upu-Upu's cargo lifts up to the sky islands,  
T+ and the market on the Landing is where it all changes hands. Aurea keeps the 
T+ vault where money and treasure are stored - assumed safe.                    
T 3;                                                                            
I pirates;;                                                                     
A pirates_word                                                                  
T 1;Okay, lore time!                                                            
T 2;There are pirates on Galene's sea, yes - and they hide their treasure on the
T+ islands. Which islands, and where, nobody honest knows, which is why every   
T+ island has a rumour about it. Aurea's vault exists half because of them.     
T 3;                                                                            
I landing;;                                                                     
A landing_word;landing_2nd                                                      
T 1;Okay, lore time!                                                            
T 2;The Landing - the island at the centre, and yours. It's a portal: the real  
T+ world on one side, Eternias on the other, and you're the one who crosses.    
T+ Home base between journeys - a harbour, the market, my old lighthouse, and   
T+ its own temple like every island. Every route runs from there and back.      
T 3;                                                                            
I life_gra;;                                                                    
A isle_amicus;life_word                                                         
S Life on Gra happens in pairs - fishing, mending, singing; a merfolk alone is  
S+ assumed to be grieving. Upper Gra sits on the volcanic ring, Lower Gra in the
S+ lagoon, joined by the coral Stair. They eat reef-fish cooked on the vents and
S+ a sour lagoon fruit nobody else can stand, and every spring at the Surfacing 
S+ the whole lagoon rises to meet the ring and couples cross the Stair together.
S+ The one thing not done: turning your back on someone speaking. Greeting:     
S+ 'Still water to you.'                                                        
I life_upuupu;;                                                                 
A isle_opux;life_word                                                           
S Upu-Upu climbs the mountain in terraces - workshops on every level, the deep  
S+ shafts at the bottom, the cargo-lift heads at the top. Shifts, whistles,     
S+ hammers; the hammers keep the rhythm Galene set, if you listen. Mountain-root
S+ stew, bread that keeps a month, tea you could stand a spoon in. Once a year  
S+ on Bell-Day nobody works and everyone complains about it by noon. The one    
S+ rule: nobody works through the bell - Opux rings it himself. Greeting: 'Hands
S+ steady.'                                                                     
I life_aurea;;                                                                  
A isle_hord;life_word                                                           
S Aurea counts - coins, feathers, favours - and counts them out loud. The Vault 
S+ Town is built around and partly inside the bank; the griffins keep eyries on 
S+ the cliffs and fly the sky-island mail. They eat what the lifts bring up,    
S+ plus a wind-cured cheese the griffins are inexplicably proud of. At year's   
S+ end, at the Forgiving, the bank publicly cancels every debt between islands  
S+ that has turned into a grudge. Not done here: lending to a friend at         
S+ interest. Greeting: 'Enough and to spare.'                                   
I life_castalia;;                                                               
A isle_elena;life_word                                                          
S No town on Castalia - houses among the trees, each a short walk from a spring,
S+ and Galene's temple where the springs run hottest. Days are measured by how  
S+ many springs you've sat at, not by what you've done; visitors find that      
S+ infuriating for about a week. Spring-warm broths, forest greens, and Elena's 
S+ bitter bark tea for most things. On Steam-Night, midwinter, every spring is  
S+ uncovered at once and the forest vanishes into warm fog. The one thing you   
S+ can be sent away for: selling a cure. Greeting: 'Warm springs to you.'       
I life_waterford;;                                                              
A isle_musix;life_word                                                          
S Waterford is one long village along a river, every garden gate unlatched, a   
S+ festival ground at each end so there's always a party at one of them. It     
S+ talks constantly - meals run two hours and are mostly conversation. Pies,    
S+ cider, three breads at every meal, and a harvest cake that takes four        
S+ families. At Long Table, midsummer, the whole village eats down the middle of
S+ the road and nobody may sit next to family. A latched gate means you've      
S+ stopped talking to someone, and the neighbours come round to find out who.   
S+ Greeting: 'Come in, the gate's open.'                                        
I life_idea;;                                                                   
A isle_mcjoy;life_word                                                          
S Idea has no towns, only squares - you live on a square and move house when the
S+ game says so, and everyone's fine with that. The lift-head is the only fixed 
S+ point, which is why it's called Start. Play, the way it was before Meister   
S+ Einsatz: score kept for the pleasure of it and forgotten by evening. Small   
S+ bright sweet food eaten in rounds. Reset, whenever it falls, sends every     
S+ piece back to Start and begins the whole island again. The rule: no score    
S+ kept past sundown. Greeting: 'Your move.'                                    
I life_petros;;                                                                 
A isle_andron;life_word                                                         
S One old town with one line down the middle. The light side is stone, glass,   
S+ roof gardens; the shadow side is the same town with the lights off and the   
S+ smoke on. Andron's house straddles the line and he sleeps on whichever side  
S+ needs him. Petros builds and mends; bread and roast on the light side, the   
S+ same recipes cooked worse on the other, which is how Andron measures         
S+ progress. On Line-Day everyone spends a day on the far side from where they  
S+ live. Not done: letting a thing stay broken more than a season - Andron just 
S+ turns up with tools. Greeting: 'Which side today?'                           
I life_ameno;;                                                                  
A isle_spark;life_word                                                          
S No towns on Ameno - it's the mirror library and the paths to it, and the paths
S+ are wherever you're sure they are. Its people are ghosts, or near enough:    
S+ beings of light who spend their days reading themselves in the mirrors. Bring
S+ your own food and eat it standing; sitting on Ameno is a commitment. The     
S+ Clearing comes without warning - the vortex goes still for an hour, and      
S+ everyone stops; that's the whole festival. Not done: lying in the library.   
S+ The mirrors simply show it. Greeting: 'Be still.'                            
I villain_amicus;;                                                              
A villain_amicus                                                                
S The Undertow - not a person: a current under Gra's lagoon that pulls couples  
S+ apart one small drift at a time. The Weaver's work in Gra. Amicus drove it   
S+ back to the deep water, but it rises whenever people stop surfacing to talk. 
S+ Defeated isn't gone.                                                         
I villain_opux;;                                                                
A villain_opux                                                                  
S The false foreman - the Weaver as a job that never ends. A voice that said    
S+ 'one more shift' until the dwarves forgot what the shifts were for. Driven   
S+ off the Terraces; he waits at the bottom of the deepest shaft, and a dwarf   
S+ who works through the bell can still hear him counting.                      
I villain_hord;;                                                                
A villain_hord                                                                  
S The Zinsmeister - interest without end, the Weaver as compounding. He made    
S+ sea-coins worth less every day and Hord worth less than his vault. Driven    
S+ from the bank; his ledger is kept in a locked room, because the numbers in it
S+ are still true, and Hord says burning a true thing doesn't make it false.    
I villain_elena;;                                                               
A villain_elena                                                                 
S Dr. Krallus - health as a product, the Weaver as a clinic that needs you sick.
S+ He turned two of Castalia's healing houses into shops and Elena into a woman 
S+ who could look at pain and see a price. Gone from the temples, clinics shut. 
S+ He's beyond the Fog Moor, and an elf who starts selling cures finds the path 
S+ across suddenly easy.                                                        
I villain_musix;;                                                               
A villain_musix                                                                 
S Frau Zwietracht - discord as a guest, the Weaver as the friend who tells you  
S+ what your family really thinks of you. She made Waterford stop talking one   
S+ kitchen at a time. Driven out of the village; she lives at the quiet end of  
S+ the river, and any hobbit who latches a gate finds her at the door next      
S+ morning, friendly as ever.                                                   
I villain_mcjoy;;                                                               
A villain_mcjoy                                                                 
S Meister Einsatz - the stake: the Weaver as the moment play needs a loser to   
S+ feel like it mattered. He turned every game on Idea into one you could lose  
S+ your house at, and MC Joy into the one who ran the table. Driven off the     
S+ board; he keeps a table in the shadow under Idea, and a pixie who keeps score
S+ past sundown starts to hear the dice.                                        
I villain_andron;;                                                              
A villain_andron                                                                
S Direktor Truebsal - neglect with a title, the Weaver as the manager who defers
S+ every repair. He didn't break Petros; he let it break, one uncleaned window  
S+ at a time, and called it prudence. Driven from the shadow side's town hall;  
S+ he keeps an office in the smoke, and anyone who lets something stay broken   
S+ past a season finds his memo on the doorstep.                                
I opinion_amicus;;                                                              
A think_word;ask_amicus                                                         
S Loses at everything and has the best time. My favourite opponent.             
I opinion_opux;;                                                                
A think_word;ask_opux                                                           
S Made him play once. He read the rules for an hour, then beat everyone. Never  
S+ again.                                                                       
I opinion_hord;;                                                                
A think_word;ask_hord                                                           
S Won't bet, won't play for stakes, won't lose. Boring! Also correct. Don't tell
S+ him.                                                                         
I opinion_elena;;                                                               
A think_word;ask_elena                                                          
S Says I'm medicine. I've decided to take that as a compliment and not ask about
S+ the dose.                                                                    
I opinion_musix;;                                                               
A think_word;ask_musix                                                          
S If we ever host a festival together, warn the neighbouring islands.           
I opinion_andron;;                                                              
A think_word;ask_andron                                                         
S Plays a long game. Very long. He's still building the board.                  
I opinion_spark;;                                                               
A think_word;ask_spark                                                          
S The one game I can't win: she just looks at you until you tell the truth.     
S+ Terrible at parties.                                                         
I rumor;;                                                                       
A rumor_word                                                                    
I proverb;;                                                                     
A proverb_word                                                                  
S Still water, whole island.                                                    
S Half-done tools rust.                                                         
S A latched gate is a question.                                                 
S Count the feathers before the coins.                                          
S The moor is easy for the ones who shouldn't cross it.                         
S No score after sundown.                                                       
S Same town, both sides.                                                        
S The mirror that smiles first is lying.                                        
S Nobody crosses the Stair alone.                                               
S She is in the sparkle, if you look.                                           
S Galene is quiet, not gone.                                                    
I daypart;;                                                                     
A daypart_word                                                                  
S Time's Tchaika's business - she flies over the whole realm and watches the    
S+ light change.                                                                
S I don't keep track of the day or the hour. Tchaika does.                      
I weekday;;                                                                     
A weekday_word;day_word                                                         
S Time's Tchaika's business - she flies over the whole realm and watches the    
S+ light change.                                                                
S I don't keep track of the day or the hour. Tchaika does.                      
